{#- News card macros (N4).

    Two card types, both deliberately NOT the R3 figure card:

      update(item, level)  — an Uncost movement update: date and its one
                             news label on the date row, title, body.
      costwatch(row)       — a Cost Watch item, built on the SAME card
                             structure: publisher and date on the eyebrow row,
                             the claim as the card body, "Read at <domain> →",
                             and exactly one label, Reported.

    N6 folds the two into one shape. A Cost Watch row carries no headline of
    its own — the claim IS the summary — so the card has no title slot to fill
    and none is invented. That is the only structural difference between the
    two cards, and it is a property of the data, not of the layout.

    `level` is the heading level for an update's title. Both news routes put
    their items directly under the introband h2, so both pass 3; the parameter
    stays because the level belongs to the page, not to the macro.

    Two label vocabularies live under /news/ (C4, sweep 2026-10-10), one per
    card type:
      Reported                         — Cost Watch items: a price published
                                         by the linked source, on a date.
      Update / Perspective / Correction — Uncost's own updates (C2/C3); every
                                         item in _data/news.js carries exactly
                                         one, and the data file fails the build
                                         otherwise.
    The receipts vocabulary (Confirmed / Estimate / Scenario / Needs refresh)
    never appears here; Reported never appears outside /news/ (nor in
    sources/register.csv); and the news labels never appear outside /news/.
    All three are enforced at build time by the news-label guard in
    eleventy.config.js. Like Reported, the news labels carry no colour of their
    own: the word is the meaning. -#}

{% macro update(item, level) -%}
<article class="up-item" data-news-item id="{{ item.slug }}">
  <div class="up-meta"><div class="date">{{ item.date }}</div><span class="lbl lbl--{{ item.label | lower }}">{{ item.label }}</span></div>
  <h{{ level }}>{{ item.title }}</h{{ level }}>
  <p>{{ item.body }}</p>
</article>
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro costwatch(row) -%}
<a class="cw" href="{{ row.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-source="{{ row.source_id }}" data-news-item>
  <div class="src"><span>{{ row.publisher }}</span><span>{{ row.data_period }}</span></div>
  <p>{{ row.display_caption }}</p>
  <div class="cw-foot">
    <span class="ext">Read at {{ row.url.split("/")[2] | replace("www.", "") }} &rarr;</span>
    <span class="lbl lbl--reported">Reported</span>
  </div>
</a>
{%- endmacro %}
